  "question": {
    "text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> long string is fixed at both ends. It has a mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;and vibrates in its first overtone under tension. Also given is a closed pipe which is&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> long which vibrates in its fundamental frequency. When both of these are sounded simultaneously, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> beats per second are heard. It is also observed that decreasing the tension in the string also decreases the beat frequency. What is the tension (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>) in the string? [Given, speed of sound in air is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>360</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "59.29",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>kg</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mtext>st&#160;</mtext></msup></math> overtone,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/abs/bd3625fe-696c-4fdf-868b-f043979c5d38-10.JPG\" style=\"width: 147px; height: 94px;\" /><br />Pipe in fundamental frequency, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>360</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/abs/1e111a34-03a4-4668-b7b5-c5ba39013803-11.JPG\" style=\"width: 112px; height: 181px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> By decreasing the tension, beat<br />frequency is decreased.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi>T</mi><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>360</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mn>25</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>308</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><mn>1000</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>59</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p>",
